%% How the project's documentation fits together (post-consolidation).
%% There is no manual changelog and no approval-gate process any more:
%% git history + merged PRs are the changelog; the docs below each own one job.
graph TD
    subgraph Front door
        README[README.md<br/>what it is, architecture,<br/>findings, status]
    end

    subgraph For contributors and agents
        PLAN[PLAN.md<br/>forward roadmap]
        AGENTS[AGENTS.md + CLAUDE.md<br/>how to work here]
        ARCH[dev/docs/architecture.md<br/>design overview]
    end

    subgraph The measured record
        CHECK[dev/progress/checkpoint.md<br/>live status snapshot]
        FIND[dev/progress/*.md<br/>durable findings A/Bs]
        BENCH[dev/benchmarks/cross-machine-results.md<br/>solve rates by machine]
        LEDGER[solutions/README.md<br/>oracle-verified ledger]
    end

    GIT[(git history + merged PRs<br/>the changelog)]

    README --> PLAN
    README --> ARCH
    README -->|summarises| FIND
    README -->|summarises| BENCH
    AGENTS -->|points to| CHECK
    CHECK -->|cites| FIND
    FIND -->|roll up into| BENCH
    FIND -->|record verified answers in| LEDGER
    GIT -.supersedes any manual changelog.-> CHECK

    style README fill:#f9f,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style CHECK fill:#bbf,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style BENCH fill:#bfb,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
    style GIT fill:#eee,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px
